From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:01:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wined3d: Remove the Vulkan pipelines made with a shader
 module when it goes.

Graphics pipelines are cached by the handles of their shader modules.
When a shader went, its modules were destroyed and the contexts let go of
them, but the pipelines made with them stayed in the cache; a module made
later can be given the same handle, and then the stale pipeline is found
and a shader long gone is run.  Drawing the same thing with shaders
released one after another gave different results depending on which
shaders had been made before.

The pipelines made with a module are now taken out of the cache, and
destroyed once the command buffer is done, as the module goes.  With the
Vulkan renderer the d3d11 tests go from 303 failures to 12 here, with this
and the per-sample fixes just before together; many of the tests make and
release shaders in loops.  Four of ps_ibfe's cases marked todo now pass
with both renderers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit fc2489e2fedddf05f902c79eaf673940756a1f86)

